<github-data-json>
{
  "title": "Coordinators C05c: Lease manager",
  "body": "Part of #902. Slice C05c is the lease manager. It provides:\n- `acquire`, renew, `update` and `release` for one claim ref, keyed on the logical run;\n- generation-bound handles required for every mutation;\n- one mutex per ref;\n- GitHub-time decisions from #951;\n- durable intents through #952;\n- the renewal loop.\n\nIt has no run wiring: #956 guards writes with it, and #960 and #963 acquire through it.\n\nBlocked by #950\nBlocked by #951\nBlocked by #952\n\n## Invariants\n1. **One holder per generation.** GitHub's `updateRefs` compare-and-swap decides every acquisition.\n2. **Handles bind mutations to an identity.**\n   - `acquire` returns a `LeaseHandle { repo, ref, run, member, generation }`.\n   - `update`, `release` and `windowOpen` require one.\n   - Under the mutex, a handle whose run, member or generation doesn't match the row's confirmed `held` ownership is **obsolete**. It is rejected before any GitHub or SQLite change, so a delayed callback from generation 1 can't touch generation 2.\n3. **Leases are keyed on the logical run.**\n   - **Same run** (`want.run === tip.run`): a new generation continues it and inherits the tip's `checkpoint` (the hand-off and adoption case).\n   - **A different run on a released tip:** allowed only when the tip's `status` is outside `ISSUE_CLAIM_STATUSES` (src/db/store.ts ~390: `queued`, `waiting`, `running`, `waiting_input`, `needs_human`). It starts a fresh lineage with nothing inherited. `TERMINAL_STATUSES` isn't the complement: it also contains `needs_human`.\n   - **A different run on a held tip,** live or expired, is always refused.\n4. **GitHub time, conservatively.**\n   - Takeover requires `expiredForTakeover` (the lower bound).\n   - Renewing an own tip after its window closed requires `renewable` (the upper bound).\n   - Each decision uses a fresh #951 sample where one is needed. Immediately before the `updateRefs` send, through #950's `beforeSend` hook, the manager recomputes the applicable predicate from current clocks with #951's `canSend`: `renewable`/window for same-generation writes, `expiredForTakeover` for takeovers. If it fails, the send is aborted (`unchanged`), and the manager re-decides, re-sampling if needed.\n5. **An expired own generation is never renewed.**\n   - Without `takeover`, `acquire` returns `superseded` and `onLost` runs.\n   - `takeover: true` is only for #963's adoption, after return quarantine. Resume and run-start paths pass `false`.\n6. **Superseded means the generation is lost, not the run.** The check uses #952's confirmed ownership, never a pending acquisition.\n7. **Uncertain is never lost.** `unchanged` and `unconfirmed` never mark a lease lost and never refresh its anchor. Only `moved` to a superseding record means lost.\n8. **Pending intents are reconciled first.**\n   - Before every operation, under the ref mutex, a row's pending intent goes through #952's `reconcileLeaseIntent`.\n   - While it stays `pending` (unresolved), the operation returns `wait` and changes nothing: it doesn't replace the intent, refresh the anchor, or report loss.\n   - The loop retries unresolved intents every tick, so an `unconfirmed` write resolves without a restart.\n9. **A failed acquisition doesn't block the next run.** When an acquisition's intent is dropped (`unchanged`) and the row was never confirmed, the manager `forgetLease`s it (#952 invariant 5). Another logical run can then acquire the same ref.\n10. **One mutex per ref** (keyed by `canonicalRepo` and ref). It covers the handle check, the fresh read, the time check, the journaled write, the classification and the confirmation. Same-holder contention (a `moved` tip with this holder, run and generation but other fields) retries from that tip and isn't loss.\n\n## Mechanism (new `src/integrations/leases.ts`)\n```ts\nexport type LeaseHandle = Readonly\u003c{ repo: string; ref: string; run: string; member: string; generation: number }\u003e;\nexport type LeaseWant = { kind: ClaimKind; number?: number; run: string; status: RunStatus; checkpoint?: string };\nexport type AcquireResult =\n  | { kind: \"held\"; handle: LeaseHandle; tip: ClaimTip }\n  | { kind: \"refused\"; reason: \"live\" | \"malformed\"; tip?: ClaimTip }\n  | { kind: \"superseded\"; tip: ClaimTip }\n  | { kind: \"wait\"; reason: string };\nexport interface LeaseManager {\n  acquire(repo: string, ref: string, want: LeaseWant, opts: { takeover: boolean }, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise\u003cAcquireResult\u003e;\n  update(h: LeaseHandle, patch: Partial\u003cPick\u003cClaimRecord, \"status\" | \"checkpoint\"\u003e\u003e): Promise\u003c\"applied\" | \"wait\" | \"lost\" | \"obsolete\"\u003e;\n  release(h: LeaseHandle, patch?: Partial\u003cPick\u003cClaimRecord, \"status\" | \"checkpoint\"\u003e\u003e): Promise\u003c\"released\" | \"wait\" | \"lost\" | \"obsolete\"\u003e;\n  windowOpen(h: LeaseHandle): boolean;         // false for obsolete handles\n  start(hooks: { active(h: LeaseHandle): boolean; onLost(h: LeaseHandle, tip: ClaimTip | null): void }): () =\u003e void;\n}\nexport async function createLeaseManager(deps: { client: ClaimClient; store: Store; clock: ClockSource; gh: GhRunner; member: string }): Promise\u003cLeaseManager\u003e;\n// runs C05b's recoverLeases first, then reports superseded rows to onLost once start() is called\n```\n#950's `write` hooks are used here: `onCommit` journals the commit SHA (`setLeaseIntentCommit`), and `beforeSend` revalidates the time sample.\n\n### `acquire` (under the mutex)\n1. Canonicalize, then read fresh.\n2. Run the superseded check against the confirmed row: return `superseded` and `markLeaseLost`.\n3. Decide from the tip:\n\n| Tip | Action |\n|---|---|\n| absent | write `held`, generation 1 |\n| `released`, same run | write `held`, generation + 1, inheriting `checkpoint` |\n| `released`, different run, tip `status` outside `ISSUE_CLAIM_STATUSES` | `forgetLease` the old run's `released` or `lost` row (#952 invariant 6), then write `held`, generation + 1, fresh lineage |\n| `released`, different run, tip `status` in `ISSUE_CLAIM_STATUSES` | `refused: live` |\n| our record at our confirmed generation, and the window is open or a fresh sample is `renewable` | renew (same generation) |\n| our record, window closed and not `renewable` | `markLeaseLost`, `onLost`. Without `takeover`: `superseded`. With `takeover`: write `held`, generation + 1, inheriting |\n| held, same run, other holder, `takeover`, `expiredForTakeover` | write `held`, generation + 1, inheriting |\n| held, same run, live, or `takeover` false | `refused: live` |\n| held, different run | `refused: live`, always |\n| malformed | `refused: malformed` |\n| no usable sample when one is needed | `wait` |\n\n4. Every write goes through `beginLeaseIntent` (the complete record), the commit, `setLeaseIntentCommit` and `write` (with `beforeSend` revalidation). Then, by outcome:\n   - **`applied`:** `confirmLease`; store the anchor in memory; return a handle.\n   - **`unchanged`:** drop the intent; if the row was never confirmed, `forgetLease` it; `wait`.\n   - **`unconfirmed`:** keep the intent; `wait`. It is reconciled before the next operation and by the loop.\n   - **`moved`:** drop the intent and re-decide once. A second `moved` is `refused`, or `superseded` for a confirmed row.\n\n### `update`, `release` and the loop\n- **`update(h)`** runs under the mutex:\n  1. reject an obsolete handle;\n  2. if the window is closed, take a sample and require `renewable` (else `lost`);\n  3. journal and write the same generation with the patch.\n- **`release(h)`** is the same, but writes `state: released` and keeps `checkpoint` unless patched. Its intent is the one #952 replays after a crash.\n- **`start`:** every 3 minutes, `update` each confirmed `held` handle whose `active` hook is true. After a detected suspend, renewal happens on the first tick after waking. `lost` calls `onLost`.\n\n## Tests\n- **Fakes:** #950's fake GitHub, fake `Date` samples, injected `ClockSource`s, and a wall source that throws if called.\n- **Two coordinators** are two managers with two stores in one process; they share no module state.\n- **The mutation check:** with #950's **unconditional-ref-write** mutant, tests 1 and 3 must fail. (A mutant that only skips the `beforeOid` check isn't enough: the fake's fast-forward rule alone could still pick one winner.)\n\n1. **Concurrent create:** one manager is `held` at generation 1, and the other is `refused: live`.\n2. **Released, by run:**\n   - The same run gets generation + 1, inheriting `checkpoint`.\n   - A different run on a `succeeded` tip gets a fresh lineage.\n   - A different run on a `needs_human` tip is refused.\n3. **Takeover:**\n   - With a lower bound 9:59 after the tip: refused; at 10:00: `held` at generation + 1, inheriting.\n   - No usable sample: `wait`.\n   - Two takers: one wins.\n4. **An own expired tip:** `update` with a closed window and a non-`renewable` sample is `lost`, and never renews. `acquire` without `takeover` is `superseded`; with `takeover`, it gets generation + 1.\n5. **Obsolete handles (review finding):**\n   - Generation 1's handle is held by a delayed callback while the same member acquires generation 2.\n   - `update(h1)` and `release(h1)` return `obsolete`.\n   - No GitHub request is made, and the SQLite row is unchanged.\n6. **Revalidation before send:**\n   - The sample is usable at decision time, and then 5 s of suspend pass before `beforeSend`.\n   - The send is aborted; the manager re-samples and re-decides.\n   - No `updateRefs` used the stale sample.\n7. **Uncertain outcomes:**\n   - `unchanged` and `unconfirmed` don't mark lost and don't refresh the anchor.\n   - `unconfirmed` leaves the intent for #952's recovery.\n8. **Same-holder contention:**\n   - A loop renewal and `update(h, { status: \"waiting_input\" })` race on one ref. They serialize, and the final tip says `waiting_input`.\n   - A forced same-holder `moved` retries, and isn't loss.\n9. **Canonical repository:** `acquire(\"Owner/Repo\", …)` and `acquire(\"owner/repo\", …)` share one row and one mutex. The second waits for the first.\n10. **No cross-run takeover:** a held, expired tip for run A refuses `acquire(want.run = B, takeover: true)`.\n11. **Recovery before start:** a row #952 reports as superseded is delivered to `onLost` once, after `start`.\n12. **Suspend:** after an applied write, the window is open. With suspend-exclusive time frozen and inclusive time +2 minutes it is closed, and the next tick renews only after a `renewable` sample.\n13. **Inert:** nothing in the daemon constructs a `LeaseManager`.\n14. **Fresh lineage keeps history safe:**\n    - A different run acquiring a `succeeded` released tip forgets the old run's `released` row first, and then holds generation + 1.\n    - Against a row this member still confirms `held` for the old run, the same acquisition is refused, and the row is unchanged.\n15. **Expiry crossed while committing:**\n    - A same-generation renewal is decided at lease age 9:59 by the upper bound, and the commit POST takes 2 s with no suspend.\n    - `beforeSend` refuses, and no `updateRefs` is sent.\n    - The re-decision finds the generation expired: the renewal is `lost`, and `onLost` runs.\n16. **`unconfirmed` resolved without a restart:**\n    - An `update` ends `unconfirmed`, and the next `update` (fake still unreadable) returns `wait` with the intent unchanged and no anchor refresh.\n    - The fake becomes readable, and the next loop tick reconciles it to `applied`.\n    - A following `update` proceeds normally.\n17. **Run B after A's failed first acquisition:**\n    - Run A's acquisition of an absent ref fails before send, and A ends.\n    - Run B's `acquire` of the same ref succeeds at generation 1.\n\n## Compatibility\n- Inert until a wiring slice constructs it.\n- No migration beyond #952's.\n- No config and no behaviour change.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Adoption policy (#963) and capability checks (#957).\n- The guard (#956).\n- Run wiring (#960).\n- The land lock (C17 (deferred), deferred).\n\n## Budget\nAbout 180 source lines plus tests:\n- handles and the obsolete check: about 20;\n- `acquire` and its table: about 60;\n- `update` and `release`: about 25;\n- time decisions with revalidation: about 20;\n- mutex and same-holder retry: about 20;\n- loop: about 20;\n- pre-operation reconciliation, the loop retry, `forgetLease` for a never-confirmed row, and the send-time predicate: about 15.\n\nStop and report past 250.\n"
}
