[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/integrations/leases.ts",
  "line": 82,
  "title": "Relinquishing ownership must close the local write window until authority is re-established",
  "detail": "A releases generation 1 and gets `unconfirmed`. B reads the released tip and acquires generation 2, yet A's `windowOpen(h1)` still returns true (~82, ~186), so C06's guard would authorize A's stale writes. The same happens when release returns `unchanged` and applies later, as C04 allows. Reproduced for both outcomes.\nWhen a release is attempted, close the window for that handle at once, whatever the outcome. Only a later reconciliation or reacquisition that confirms this machine's ownership may reopen it."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/integrations/leases.ts",
  "line": 49,
  "title": "Register recovered and recovery-confirmed leases for renewal",
  "detail": "`handles` starts empty (~49) and is filled only by this instance's successful writes. Recovery restores SQLite ownership without registering handles (~239). So `start({ active: () => true, \u2026 })` never renews an existing confirmed lease, or one whose acquisition recovery confirmed, and the lease expires unless the caller reacquires it. That misses the requirement to renew every active confirmed held handle. Reproduced for both restart cases: zero renewal writes on the tick.\nRebuild the renewable handle set from the store on construction and after recovery."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
  "file": "src/integrations/leases.ts",
  "line": 107,
  "title": "Reconcile a pending never-confirmed acquisition before deciding another run's acquisition",
  "detail": "A's first acquisition ends `unconfirmed` without applying. When GitHub becomes readable and shows the ref still absent, B's acquisition returns `refused` at once (~107), before reconciliation can drop A's intent and forget its never-confirmed row. Invariant 8 requires reconciliation before each operation. Reproduced: expected B to acquire generation 1, got `refused`.\nReconcile the pending intent first, then decide B's result."
 },
 {
  "id": "F4",
  "file": "test/leases.test.ts",
  "line": 138,
  "title": "Keep the race invariant assertions identical under the mutant",
  "detail": "Under the unconditional-write mutant, the race helper changes its expectation to two winners and skips the loser-refusal assertion, so both mutant tests pass while breaking tests 1 and 3's invariant. The spec requires those assertions to fail under that mutant. Keep the invariant assertions identical for real and mutant clients, and if needed add a separate meta-test that asserts the mutant run fails.\n\nRegressions (all fail at HEAD), to add to test/leases.test.ts:\n```ts\n\ntest.each([\"unconfirmed\", \"unchanged\"] as const)(\n  \"review regression: an ambiguous %s release closes the old holder's write window\",\n  async (mode) => {\n    const a = fixture();\n    const b = fixture(a.gh, other);\n    const ma = await a.create();\n    const mb = await b.create();\n    const h = held(await a.acquire(ma)).handle;\n    let unreadable = false;\n    let applyLater: (() => void) | undefined;\n    a.gh.fault = (r) => {\n      if (r.step === \"update\") {\n        applyLater = () => a.gh.apply(r);\n        if (mode === \"unconfirmed\") {\n          applyLater();\n          unreadable = true;\n        }\n        throw new Error(\"Lost release response\");\n      }\n      if (r.step === \"ref\" && unreadable) throw new Error(\"Unreadable\");\n    };\n    expect(await ma.release(h)).toBe(\"wait\");\n    expect(a.row()?.intent !== null).toBe(mode === \"unconfirmed\");\n    a.gh.fault = undefined;\n    applyLater?.();\n    expect(held(await b.acquire(mb)).handle.generation).toBe(2);\n    expect(a.row()?.confirmed?.state).toBe(\"held\");\n    expect(ma.windowOpen(h)).toBe(false);\n  },\n);\n\ntest.each([false, true])(\n  \"review regression: restart renews confirmed held ownership (recovered intent: %s)\",\n  async (pending) => {\n    const f = fixture();\n    if (pending) {\n      const tip = f.gh.seed(record);\n      f.store.beginLeaseIntent(repo, ref, want.run, {\n        op: \"acquire\",\n        before: \"0\".repeat(40),\n        record,\n        commit: tip.sha,\n      });\n    } else held(await f.acquire(await f.create()));\n    const manager = await f.create();\n    f.start(manager);\n    f.advance(LEASE.renewMs);\n    const writes = f.gh.calls(\"update\").length;\n    await f.tick();\n    expect(f.row()?.confirmed?.state).toBe(\"held\");\n    expect(f.gh.calls(\"update\")).toHaveLength(writes + 1);\n  },\n);\n\ntest(\"review regression: run B reconciles run A's unapplied pending acquisition first\", async () => {\n  const f = fixture();\n  const manager = await f.create();\n  let unreadable = false;\n  f.gh.fault = (r) => {\n    if (r.step === \"update\") {\n      unreadable = true;\n      throw new Error(\"Write not applied\");\n    }\n    if (r.step === \"ref\" && unreadable) throw new Error(\"Unreadable\");\n  };\n  expect((await f.acquire(manager)).kind).toBe(\"wait\");\n  expect(f.row()).toMatchObject({ confirmed: null, intent: { op: \"acquire\" } });\n  f.gh.fault = undefined;\n  const result = await f.acquire(manager, false, { ...want, run: \"run-b\" });\n  expect(held(result).handle.generation).toBe(1);\n  expect(f.row()).toMatchObject({ runId: \"run-b\", confirmed: { state: \"held\" }, intent: null });\n});\n\n```"
 }
